      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Upgrade to Lite Tier",
      "Anchor": "upgrade-to-lite-tier",
      "SectionPath": [],
      "Text": "Upgrade to production-ready access by moving from Development to Lite tier. Lite tier uses the same APIs as Development tier, but allows you to access verification data for all LinkedIn members instead of just developer app administrators.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Upgrade to Lite Tier",
      "Anchor": "upgrade-to-lite-tier",
      "SectionPath": [],
      "Text": "Important",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Upgrade to Lite Tier",
      "Anchor": "upgrade-to-lite-tier",
      "SectionPath": [],
      "Text": "Lite tier is identical to Development tier in terms of APIs and implementation. The only difference: you can now access all LinkedIn members instead of just developer app administrators. No code changes required!",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "How the upgrade process works",
      "Anchor": "how-the-upgrade-process-works",
      "SectionPath": [
        "How the upgrade process works"
      ],
      "Text": "End-to-end upgrade flow:",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "How the upgrade process works",
      "Anchor": "how-the-upgrade-process-works",
      "SectionPath": [
        "How the upgrade process works"
      ],
      "Text": "Submit an upgrade request from the Developer Portal.\nProvide your business details as part of the request.\nComplete a short LinkedIn survey.\nFollow the onboarding instructions provided by LinkedIn.\nOnce Lite tier access is enabled, your app can access all LinkedIn members.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "How the upgrade process works",
      "Anchor": "how-the-upgrade-process-works",
      "SectionPath": [
        "How the upgrade process works"
      ],
      "Text": "[!NOTE]",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "How the upgrade process works",
      "Anchor": "how-the-upgrade-process-works",
      "SectionPath": [
        "How the upgrade process works"
      ],
      "Text": "This process makes your integration production-ready. Your API endpoints, scopes, and implementation remain unchanged.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
